# Resibo client — environment TEMPLATE. Committed; carries names only.
#
# Everything here is PUBLIC. Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed value into the
# JavaScript bundle the browser downloads, so a credential must never appear in
# a file like this one. See resibo-plan.md §8.
#
# Nothing here is required. With no env file at all, the client talks to the
# DEPLOYED API — see src/config/env.ts — so `npm run dev` works with no local
# backend, no database and no JAVA_HOME.

# Base URL for the API, including the /api prefix.
#
# Leave unset to use the deployed API:
#   https://resibo-api.polbinsenthabyer.uk/api
#
# Set it to the relative path to use a LOCAL backend instead. vite.config.ts
# proxies /api to localhost:8083, so the browser sees one origin and CORS does
# not apply:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api
#
# Or name another origin explicitly:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8083/api
#
# ⚠️ The default points development at PRODUCTION. Harmless while the only
# call is a health check; revisit before any screen can write. The backend's
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS defaults to "*" and names http://localhost:5173, so the
# deployed API accepts the dev server today.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
